    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today\u2019s slate prioritizing heavy-hitter production in the heart of the lineup, anchored by **Josh Naylor** (64.77) and **James Wood** (64.75). **Josh Naylor** benefits from a strong matchup against Ryne Nelson, whose xERA of 4.21 allows for optimal damage in the #3 hole. Meanwhile, **James Wood** remains a priority start; despite a modest -2% penalty for the opposing pitcher\u2019s ability to suppress stolen bases, his elite lead-off positioning (+10%) and solid 0.384 xwOBA make him a foundation piece for our Roto floor. **Vinnie Pasquantino** (72.62) serves as our top offensive engine today, as the 14% platoon boost against the right-handed Rocker provides the highest ceiling among our active roster.\n\nStrategic flexibility is paramount, especially with several players carrying the \"Lineup Pending\" designation. **Corbin Carroll** (60.40) is a crucial start despite a tough matchup against Bryan Woo; while the pitcher's 3.43 xERA is daunting, the combination of **Corbin Carroll** batting in the #2 spot and his massive utility in our scarcest category, SB, outweighs the park-induced downward pressure. The most difficult bench decision involved **Kyle Karros** (54.55), who offered decent upside due to a favorable park and pitcher matchup. Ultimately, he was sidelined in favor of **Henry Bolte** (53.85) because **Henry Bolte**\u2019s superior platoon advantage against Ryan Weathers provided a higher projected efficiency floor for our total game cap management.\n\nRisks today are concentrated in the catcher and middle-infield slots. **Gabriel Moreno** (46.11) and **Jose Caballero** (45.60) are currently hovering near our \"Below floor\" threshold. With **Gabriel Moreno** facing the elite arm of Bryan Woo and **Jose Caballero** relegated to the bottom of the order with a -13% platoon penalty, these spots are high-leverage liabilities. We are watching the official lineups closely; if **Jose Caballero** or **Gabriel Moreno** are moved into more favorable spots, their efficiency will normalize, but for now, they are clear candidates to be pulled if we reach our daily game cap early.",
